{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"Pantelis23.KernRift","latestVersion":"v2.10.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Self-hosted bare-metal systems programming language and compiler","license":"Apache-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/Heniokhos-Systems/KernRift/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Self-hosted bare-metal systems programming language and compiler","license":"Apache-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/Heniokhos-Systems/KernRift/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"KernRift is a zero-dependency self-hosted compiler. The package installs two portable command-line tools — krc (the compiler) and kr (the fat-binary runner). It compiles to native x86_64 and ARM64 binaries for Linux, Windows, macOS, and Android. The compiler is written entirely in KernRift itself and produces ELF, PE, Mach-O, and fat binaries.","moniker":"kernrift","name":"KernRift","packageUrl":"https://github.com/Heniokhos-Systems/KernRift","publisher":"Pantelis Christou","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/Heniokhos-Systems/KernRift","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/Heniokhos-Systems/KernRift/releases/tag/v2.10.0","tags":["aot","arm64","bare-metal","compiler","cross-compiler","programming-language","self-hosted","systems-programming","x86_64"]}},"longDescription":"KernRift is a zero-dependency self-hosted compiler. The package installs two portable command-line tools — krc (the compiler) and kr (the fat-binary runner). It compiles to native x86_64 and ARM64 binaries for Linux, Windows, macOS, and Android. The compiler is written entirely in KernRift itself and produces ELF, PE, Mach-O, and fat binaries.","moniker":"kernrift","name":"KernRift","packageUrl":"https://github.com/Heniokhos-Systems/KernRift","publisher":"Pantelis Christou","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/Heniokhos-Systems/KernRift","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/Heniokhos-Systems/KernRift/releases/tag/v2.10.0","tags":["